The other major acute complication is hypoglycemia. Severe hypoglycemia, marked by coma or convulsions, is very frightening, and fear of hypoglycemia can be an important barrier to good glycemic control. Therefore, prevention and management are essential survival skills to be taught to the patient and family at the time of diagnosis, and reinforced frequently.

